# launch_daemon job for cloud_init_lite. Installed as
# /boot/system/settings/launch/cloud_init_lite, read by the *system*
# launch_daemon (see the note in launch-sshd about why the system context and
# not the user one -- there is no desktop on a Nitro instance).
#
# "job", not "service": this is one-shot. A service would be restarted forever
# by launch_daemon, and there is nothing to restart -- once the key is merged and
# the hostname set, the work is done. The program is idempotent anyway, so a
# re-run is harmless, but it should not be a background process that never ends.
#
# No "on <event>" condition. Haiku's launch_daemon has no
# "network is configured and has a lease" event to wait for, and inventing one is
# a bigger change than this feature deserves, so the program waits for DHCP
# itself with a bounded retry. That waiting happens here, in its own job, and
# therefore delays nothing else -- in particular sshd is a separate job and
# comes up immediately, which is what keeps a non-EC2 boot from being held up.

job x-vnd.haiku-cloud_init_lite {
	launch /boot/system/bin/cloud_init_lite
	legacy
}
